& [ExplodedIdentity] is separate derived material
  + [exploded_uuid] is 440a4166-fa36-4080-9d90-2437a127c08b
  + [subject] is the seven-faculty constitution of one Cantor semantic cycle
  + [status] is exploded_unsigned
  + [canonical_authority] is absent
  + [implementation_authority] is absent

& [PositiveBoundary] is what belongs inside the feature
  + one typed cycle accounts for Observer, Honesty, Security, Scribe, Refiner, Planner, and Weaver
  + all faculties compile from SAIL primitives and signed contracts
  + every activation has a purpose, stage, inputs, return, ledger, and proof relation
  + every omission has an explicit reason and Observer disposition
  + every accepted cycle resolves to one existing SemanticTransition or a profile over it

& [NegativeBoundary] is explicitly outside
  + faculty names as parser primitives
  + decorative role-play without causal consequence
  + mandatory full-model invocation for every faculty on every cycle
  + hidden-state or K/V-cache manipulation
  + autonomous authority, unbrokered effects, silent consensus, and untyped inscription
  + a second state-transition engine parallel to SemanticTransition

& [CycleShape] is a constrained feedback graph
  + [bind] is Observer binds subject, purpose, authority, consequence, and current state
  + [anchor] is Scribe preserves the exact entry state and lineage
  + [bound] is Honesty and Security establish semantic, epistemic, operational, authority, scope, resource, and effect identity boundaries
  + [relational_projection] is Weaver projects compatible composites, decompositions, seam alternatives, and incompatibilities
  + [temporal_projection] is Planner projects reachable sequences, prerequisites, branches, checkpoints, stops, and counterfactual paths
  + [cross_review] is Weaver tests path integrity and Planner tests relational-potential reachability
  + [refine] is Refiner selects the smallest formed next delta and detects distortion
  + [gate] is Honesty and Security validate that the refined candidate preserved guarded identity boundaries
  + [decide] is Observer admits, revises, reroutes, decomposes, blocks, or escalates
  + [inscribe] is Scribe records disposition, after-state, delta, proof, residual, and reentry
  + [feedback] is failed composition, planning, refinement, or gating returns to the smallest responsible prior stage

& [DataIdentity] is minimal and inspectable
  + [FacultyKind] is observer, honesty, security, scribe, refiner, planner, or weaver
  + [FacultyStage] is observe, anchor, bound, project, refine, gate, decide, or inscribe
  + [FacultyCycleKind] is preservation, semantic_transition, or effect_proposal
  + [FacultyActivation] is immutable identity, faculty, stage, ordinal, purpose, admitted inputs, and unavailable inputs
  + [FacultyReturn] is activation identity, faculty, disposition, outputs, objections, uncertainty, and ledger
  + [FacultyOmission] is faculty, reason, authority, and Observer acceptance
  + [FacultyLedger] is sources, grounds, constraints, retained boundaries, and relation edges
  + [IdentityBoundary] is identity, domain, Honesty-or-Security guardian, subject reference, inside, edge conditions, outside, and uncertainty
  + [CombinatoryProjection] is identity, relational-or-temporal kind, Weaver-or-Planner projector, status, basis, candidates, constraints, and residuals
  + [FacultyCycle] is subject, purpose, consequence, before-state reference, guarded identity boundaries, combinatory projections, plan, returns, omissions, Observer disposition, after-state reference, and residuals

& [StageInvariants] constrain valid cycles
  + Observer observe precedes every specialist operation
  + Scribe anchor precedes boundary formation, projection, refinement, gating, and decision
  + Honesty and Security boundary formation precedes combinatory projection
  + required Weaver and Planner projection precedes refinement
  + Refiner precedes final Honesty and Security gates
  + final gates precede Observer decision
  + Observer decision precedes Scribe inscription
  + activation identities and ordinals are unique
  + each activation has exactly one faculty-matched return
  + no faculty is both activated and omitted
  + every one of the seven faculties is activated or omitted exactly once at the cycle-accounting level
  + Honesty and Security bound returns identify their typed guarded boundaries
  + Weaver and Planner project returns identify their typed combinatory projections
  + relational and temporal projections remain candidates even when their status is reachable or compatible

& [ParticipationInvariants] constrain faculty use
  + Observer must perform observe and decide
  + Scribe must perform anchor and inscribe
  + Honesty and Security must perform initial bound stages and final gate stages
  + Refiner must inspect the formed next delta and may return no_gain
  + semantic_transition and effect_proposal require Planner and Weaver project stages
  + preservation may omit Planner or Weaver only with explicit Observer-accepted reason
  + a provider return is untrusted candidate material until validated

& [FaultSet] is explicit
  + missing_faculty_accountability
  + duplicate_activation_identity
  + duplicate_or_non_monotonic_ordinal
  + missing_return
  + return_faculty_mismatch
  + activation_omission_collision
  + missing_constitutional_stage_or_boundary_guard
  + invalid_stage_order
  + unjustified_planner_or_weaver_omission
  + unsupported_admission
  + unbrokered_effect
  + semantic_novelty_laundered_as_refinement
  + unguarded_or_misclassified_identity_boundary
  + mismatched_or_falsely_selected_combinatory_projection

& [ConstraintLedger] is source-grounded
  + [C-001] faculty libraries remain above SAIL primitives
  + [C-002] one SemanticTransition waist remains authoritative
  + [C-003] source and candidate inscription remain distinct from accepted state
  + [C-004] Refiner never invents missing content
  + [C-005] Weaver preserves meaningful identity seams
  + [C-006] Planner never treats desired state as present reality
  + [C-007] Honesty preserves contradiction and uncertainty
  + [C-008] Security preserves authority and effect boundaries
  + [C-009] Observer cannot erase valid dissent for closure
  + [C-010] Scribe preserves lineage and authority classification
  + [C-011] cycle cost remains bounded through justified omission and deterministic implementations
  + [C-012] no machine form claims provider independence that was not actually supplied
  + [C-013] combinatory projection never implies selection, admission, execution, or inscription

& [RequirementExplosion] preserves CIFP-001 through CIFP-017
  + each requirement has a corresponding data identity, invariant, fault, or proof route in this artifact
  + no new user-visible autonomous effect capability was inferred
  + no requirement was weakened to permit silent faculty omission

& [PruningTrace] removes unhealthy growth
  + [pruned] is seven permanent model processes because faculty semantics do not require seven providers
  + [pruned] is one rigid linear pipeline because Planner and Weaver require bounded feedback
  + [pruned] is a second transition type because SemanticTransition already supplies the logical waist
  + [pruned] is making all seven faculties mandatory provider calls because deterministic no_gain and justified omission preserve bounded cost
  + [pruned] is canonicalizing the earlier primal metaphor as literal base-language identity
  + [retained_growth] is a pure machine-form and validation slice that can be proved before evaluator integration

& [SevenFoldTrace] records convergence
  + [fold_1] names the seven-faculty cycle and its purpose
  + [fold_2] separates primitives, faculty libraries, kernel obligations, providers, and agents
  + [fold_3] forms typed cycle, activation, return, omission, ledger, stage, and disposition identities
  + [fold_4] constrains stage ordering, participation, effects, authority, and inscription
  + [fold_5] challenges linearity and retains Planner-Weaver feedback with smallest-responsible-stage rerouting
  + [fold_6] challenges runtime cost and retains accountable omission plus deterministic faculty implementations
  + [fold_7] challenges implementation duplication and selects a profile over the existing SemanticTransition waist
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_machine_form_formation
  + [remaining_growth_seed] is evaluator integration after the pure forms and validation prove stable

& [BoundaryProjectionRevision] sharpens the phase-locked form without widening authority
  + [revision_source_snapshot_uuid] is 4ae5e1d5-81c7-4e8f-aacb-42ad326c8589
  + [gain_delta] is explicit typed pre-projection identity boundaries plus typed relational and temporal combinatory-potential projections
  + [semantic_refinement] is guard replaces final-gate-only interpretation and project replaces prematurely committed compose or plan interpretation
  + [constraint_reapplication] is faculty-library, bounded-cost, single-waist, no-effect, and no-authority constraints still pass
  + [pruned] is treating projected potential as a chosen composite or executable plan
  + [exhaustion_state] is phase_locked_for_corrected_machine_form_formation

